From: Zurker <91011862+hershate@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 01:37:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Papo: batch 127 self-exclusion of the wire's own position
 from the mark closure - a wire's own POWER is not an input to its own
 calculation (calculateTargetStrength reads neighbours only), so the
 self-notification arriving from its own flip's fan-out is provably redundant
 (skip-safe: inputs unchanged since the evaluation that just set that POWER;
 any interleaved input change re-marks through the existing closure hooks);
 the freshly-placed wire's first onPlace evaluation (stored POWER is the
 placement default, not a computed value - the batch 126 self-marking
 rationale) is instead guaranteed by the evaluator gate: updateShape==true
 arrives exactly from RedStoneWireBlock.onPlace (!oldState.is(wire)), so those
 evaluations always proceed and additionally clear any stale dirty bit at pos
 (the synchronized stripe lock gives the happens-before edge against
 concurrent WorldGenRegion marks); net effect: the
 one-extra-no-change-evaluation correctness cost of batch 126 (~3714/tick in
 the N=441 macro, 12.1% of notifications) becomes skippable


diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/redstone/DefaultRedstoneWireEvaluator.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/redstone/DefaultRedstoneWireEvaluator.java
index ddfa2c4751a0bc040b539b936821df6893b5197f..5bc66377c2d5a798c89861850e33caabd9d6b7e8 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/redstone/DefaultRedstoneWireEvaluator.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/redstone/DefaultRedstoneWireEvaluator.java
@@ -33,10 +33,18 @@ public class DefaultRedstoneWireEvaluator extends RedstoneWireEvaluator {
         // evaluation is skipped, equivalent by construction.
         // Survey measured 85.0% of ring-oscillator evaluations taking this branch
         // (77.5% in the post-closure-fix 4-cell verify leg).
-        if (level.papoWireDirty.evalEntry(pos)) {
+        // Batch 127: updateShape == true marks the onPlace-driven evaluation of a
+        // freshly placed wire (blockAdded path in RedStoneWireBlock) - its stored
+        // POWER is the placement default, not a computed value, so this evaluation
+        // must ALWAYS proceed (marking is self-excluded since batch 127, and even
+        // before that the placement mark could race ahead of the evaluator).
+        if (!updateShape && level.papoWireDirty.evalEntry(pos)) {
             io.papermc.paper.util.PapoTickProfile.addCount("rs.wireEvalSkipped", 1);
             return;
         }
+        if (updateShape) {
+            level.papoWireDirty.evalEntry(pos); // clear any stale dirty bit: this evaluation supersedes it
+        }
         io.papermc.paper.util.PapoTickProfile.addCount("rs.wireEvalRuns", 1); // Papo - batch 125 counter (now counts proceeded evaluations; diagnostic-only, papo.tickProfile-gated)
         // Papo end - batch 126
         int i = this.calculateTargetStrength(level, pos);
